Subject: Disc file times: one fixed time for every game-disc file

The game's Z: cache (save\Cache) holds copies of disc files, and the game decides it is stale by the
files' times: it re-copies a cache file whose time differs from the disc file's. A disc file reported
the host file's time (the install time), so after a fresh install every disc file was "newer" than the
cache, the game re-copied the whole cache, and that re-copy fought the menu music streaming from the
disc and failed on a sharing violation, stopping the loader thread. A disc is read-only and every
install of the same disc agrees on its XBE header TimeDate, so the runtime now reports that one value
(the host sets it with xbox_SetDiscTime before any guest file I/O) as the creation, access, write and
change time of every game-disc file, as XDVDFS reports one volume time for the whole disc.
xbox_host_path_is_disc tells the file layer which host paths are on the disc (the game folder) rather
than the save folder; it strips the \\?\ extended-length prefix that GetFinalPathNameByHandleW puts on
a handle's path, so the handle-based time queries stamp disc files too.

